  "methodologyBasedOn": "Based on:",
  "methodologyIntro": "SmartNutri checks each packaged food against its label and each family member's profile using fixed rules. An AI only explains the result; it never decides it. This is information, not medical advice.",
  "methodologyMetaDescription": "How SmartNutri checks packaged food for each family member: the fixed rules, their thresholds and sources. Information, not medical advice.",
  "methodologyPendingReview": "These thresholds are working values, pending review by a clinician.",
  "methodologySectionAllergensDescription": "We look for each allergen's ingredient names and for the pack's allergen statements. If the ingredients can't be read, we say the label is unclear, never OK.",
  "methodologySectionAllergensTitle": "Allergens",
  "methodologySectionBloodSugarDescription": "For members managing blood sugar (diabetes, prediabetes or PCOS), we flag products with a lot of sugar, or a lot of carbohydrate per serving, and high salt or saturated fat.",
  "methodologySectionBloodSugarTitle": "Blood sugar",
  "methodologySectionBuildMuscleDescription": "For members who want to build muscle, we note products with good protein for their calories. This goal never adds a caution or an avoid. In the food log, adults with a weight see a daily protein guide based on body weight. If you have kidney disease, ask your doctor before eating more protein.",
  "methodologySectionBuildMuscleTitle": "Build muscle",
  "methodologySectionChildDescription": "For children, we compare the sugar in 100 g or one serving with a daily sugar limit for their age.",
  "methodologySectionChildTitle": "Children",
  "methodologySectionClaimsDescription": "We check claims such as \"sugar free\" or \"high protein\" against the label values and the FSSAI limits.",
  "methodologySectionClaimsTitle": "Front-of-pack claims",
  "methodologySectionCustomAlertsDescription": "Ingredients a member asked to be told about, such as palm oil or maida. These are preferences, so there is no source to cite.",
  "methodologySectionCustomAlertsTitle": "Your ingredient alerts",
  "methodologySectionDailyLimitsDescription": "In the food log, we add up the sugar and salt logged for each member in a day and compare the totals with a daily limit for their age. Protein is shown as progress towards a daily target. Labels give total sugar, not only added sugar, so this can warn more than needed.",
  "methodologySectionDailyLimitsTitle": "Daily limits",
  "methodologySectionDietDescription": "We look for ingredients that don't fit a member's diet (vegetarian, eggetarian, vegan or Jain) and check the green or brown mark on the pack.",
  "methodologySectionDietTitle": "Diet",
  "methodologySectionHighInDescription": "A product is marked high in a nutrient when its amount per 100 g or 100 ml is at or above these limits.",
  "methodologySectionHighInTitle": "High in sugar, fat, saturated fat or salt",
  "methodologySectionHypertensionDescription": "For members with high blood pressure, we flag products with a lot of salt.",
  "methodologySectionHypertensionTitle": "Blood pressure",
  "methodologySectionInfantDescription": "For babies and toddlers, we flag added sugar, added salt, honey and caffeine, and high sugar or salt.",
  "methodologySectionInfantTitle": "Babies and toddlers",
  "methodologySectionNutriscore2023Description": "We calculate a Nutri-Score grade from the label, using the 2023 update of the method. It is calculated by SmartNutri; it is not an FSSAI rating.",
  "methodologySectionNutriscore2023Title": "Nutri-Score (calculated by SmartNutri)",
  "methodologySectionSupplementsDescription": "Protein powders, whey and other supplements get no Nutri-Score grade and are never suggested as alternatives. We still check allergens, diet, claims and each member's rules, and add a caution for children and teenagers (an avoid under 2).",
  "methodologySectionSupplementsTitle": "Supplements",
  "methodologySectionWeightLossDescription": "For members losing weight, we flag energy-dense products and low Nutri-Score grades, and note products with good protein for their calories.",
  "methodologySectionWeightLossTitle": "Weight loss",
  "methodologySourcesTitle": "Sources",
